{"name":"Almond Kiss","hex":"#f6e3d4","fetched":"2026-10-21","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"almond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The seed within the drupe of a small deciduous tree in family Rosaceae, Prunus amygdalus, considered a culinary nut.","The tree that produces almonds."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Brownish, resembling the colour of an almond nut."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/almond"},{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Almond","blocks":[{"text":"The almond is a species of tree from the genus Prunus. Along with the peach, it is classified in the subgenus Amygdalus, distinguished from the other subgenera by corrugations on the woody shell (endocarp) surrounding the seed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg/330px-Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Almond","wikidata":"Q15545507"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Kiss%2C_Love_kiss%2C_Romance%2C_People_kissing%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Kiss%2C_Love_kiss%2C_Romance%2C_People_kissing%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss","wikidata":"Q7307"},{"title":"List of Crayola crayon colors","blocks":[{"text":"Since the introduction of Crayola drawing crayons by Binney & Smith in 1903, more than 200 colors have been produced in a wide variety of assortments. The table below represents all of the colors found in regular Crayola assortments from 1903 to the present. Since the introduction of fluorescent crayons in the 1970s, the standard colors have been complemented by a number of specialty crayon assortments, represented in subsequent tables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Crayola1.jpg/330px-Crayola1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Crayola_crayon_colors","wikidata":"Q6568034"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg/500px-Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg/1280px-Almonds_-_in_shell%2C_shell_cracked_open%2C_shelled%2C_blanched.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","s